  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Danya has a rooted tree with NNN nodes (numbered 111 through NNN). Node 111 is the root and for each iii (2≤i≤N2 \\le i \\le N2≤i≤N), the parent of the iii-th node is pip_ipi​. For each valid iii, the iii-th node also has a value aia_iai​.\n\nDanya really loves his tree and wants to play with it. You should answer his QQQ queries. In each query:\n\n\nYou are given two integers XXX and DDD.\nConsider the set SSS of all nodes vvv that lie in the subtree of node XXX (including XXX) such that the distance between XXX and vvv does not exceed DDD.\nThe answer to this query is the number of different values ava_vav​ among all v∈Sv \\in Sv∈S.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤51 \\le T \\le 51≤T≤5",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤pi≤i−11 \\le p_i \\le i-11≤pi​≤i−1 for each valid iii",
      "1≤ai≤N1 \\le a_i \\le N1≤ai​≤N for each valid iii",
      "1≤Q≤2⋅1051 \\le Q \\le 2 \\cdot 10^51≤Q≤2⋅105",
      "0≤x,d≤4⋅1050 \\le x, d \\le 4 \\cdot 10^50≤x,d≤4⋅105",
      "1≤X≤N1 \\le X \\le N1≤X≤N",
      "0≤D≤N0 \\le D \\le N0≤D≤N",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (16 points):** N,Q≤1,000N, Q \\le 1,000N,Q≤1,000",
      "**Subtask #2 (24 points):** the tree is a bamboo, i.e. pi=i−1p_i = i-1pi​=i−1 for each valid iii"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains N−1N-1N−1 space-separated integers p2,p3,…,pNp_2, p_3, \\ldots, p_Np2​,p3​,…,pN​.\nThe third line contains NNN space-separated integers a1,a2,…,aNa_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_Na1​,a2​,…,aN​.\nThe fourth line contains a single integer QQQ.\nQQQ lines follow. Each of these lines contains two space-separated integers xxx and ddd describing a query; the parameters XXX and DDD can be computed in the following way:\n\nLet's denote the answer to the previous query by ansansans (ans=0ans = 0ans=0 if this is the first query).\nThen, X=x⊕ansX = x \\oplus ansX=x⊕ans and D=d⊕ansD = d \\oplus ansD=d⊕ans, where ⊕\\oplus⊕ denotes the bitwise XOR operator.",
    "outputFormat": "For each query, print a single line containing one integer ― the answer to the query.",
